*"Sir, sed means stream editor. We use it mainly to edit text in a file or input stream automatically, without opening the file in an editor. For example, it is very good for search‑and‑replace operations.

Difference from awk:

    awk is mainly used for working with structured text, like splitting lines into columns and printing or processing fields.

    sed is mainly used for editing text, like replacing, deleting, or inserting lines.

